  "articleBody": "Property damage can be really jarring, and knowing what to do first can make a huge difference. When disaster strikes, your immediate actions are crucial for both your safety and the success of any insurance claims. First things first: ensure everyone is safe and, if necessary, evacuate. Once immediate safety is secure, you need to assess the damage visually without putting yourself at risk. Next, report the damage to your insurance company as soon as reasonably possible. Many policies require prompt reporting, often within 24-48 hours. Document everything with photos and videos before any cleanup begins – this is vital evidence. Then, it's about emergency mitigation; this means taking steps to prevent further damage, like boarding up windows or stopping a leak. Don't skip this, as it can prevent secondary issues and might be required by your insurer. Finally, contact a reputable restoration service, like HH Remodeling LLC, who can provide a damage assessment, manage the mitigation, and help with the repair/rebuild. We can work with you and your insurer to get your property back to normal. Reach out for quick support when you need it most.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}